From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:41:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: qcom-hw: CPRh: fix OSM parameter generation after
 the genpd attach

- Without the required-OPP linking the CPU device isn't attached to the
  OPP table yet when the OSM parameters are generated: CPR3 populated
  the shared table through the genpd virtual device. Count and walk the
  OPPs on that device instead.
- devm_pm_domain_attach_list() returns the number of attached domains;
  don't hand that back to the caller as an error.
---
 drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c b/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c
index 8d6998dafa73..46b0dcc3d72c 100644
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c
@@ -550,8 +550,13 @@ static int qcom_cpufreq_gen_params(struct device *cpu_dev,
 	if (!cpr_data)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, -ENODATA, "Cannot get CPR data\n");
 
-	/* Get the count of available OPPs coming from the power domain */
-	gpd_opp_cnt = dev_pm_opp_get_opp_count(cpu_dev);
+	/*
+	 * Get the count of available OPPs coming from the power domain. CPR3
+	 * populated the (shared) CPU OPP table through the genpd virtual
+	 * device; the CPU device itself is only attached to it later, when the
+	 * LUT gets read back.
+	 */
+	gpd_opp_cnt = dev_pm_opp_get_opp_count(*genpd_cpr_vdev);
 	if (gpd_opp_cnt < 2) {
 		ret = gpd_opp_cnt > 0 ? -EINVAL : gpd_opp_cnt;
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "Got invalid number of OPPs\n");
@@ -598,7 +603,7 @@ static int qcom_cpufreq_gen_params(struct device *cpu_dev,
 		 * defined frequency, so we quit the loop gracefully without
 		 * signaling any error, as this is the expected behavior.
 		 */
-		genpd_opp = dev_pm_opp_find_freq_ceil(cpu_dev, &rate);
+		genpd_opp = dev_pm_opp_find_freq_ceil(*genpd_cpr_vdev, &rate);
 		if (IS_ERR(genpd_opp))
 			break;
 
@@ -695,7 +700,8 @@ static int qcom_cpufreq_gen_params(struct device *cpu_dev,
 
 	*num_entries = i;
 
-	return ret;
+	/* ret still holds the number of attached PM domains */
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static inline u32 qcom_cpufreq_acd_regbit(u8 acd_reg_offset)
-- 
